WEBVTT

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.360
<b>Team Bagra</b>

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.360
<b>Enemy?                              The battle begins!                              Enemy</b>

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.360
<b>Team ?                       Team Taiki                    Team Kiriha</b>

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.360
Mysterious
Girl

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.360
<b>Enemy?                                    Enemy?

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.360
Rival

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.360
Protagonist

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.330
<b>Current Location of Taiki's Team</b>

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.330
<b>Island Zone</b>

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.490
My name is Taiki Kudou.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:20.020
I was taken to this mysterious 
place called the Digital World,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.470
where I met Shoutmon and 
lots of other Digimon.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.110
This world is having a lot of trouble 
with the attacking Bagra Army.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.480
In our battle with Neptunemon 
in the Island Zone,

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.620
we managed to defeat the Mantaraymon 
fleet and Octomon, but...

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.920
<i>Buddy Blaster!</i>

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.810
Who will be the ones to obtain 
this Zone's Code Crown?

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.120
Our team?

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:50.820
Or the Bagra Army?

00:00:51.910 --> 00:01:00.390
<b>The DigiMemory Shines!</b>

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.070
The DigiMemory Shines!

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:09.280
I'm telling you, the, uh... Co... Co...

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.690
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.200
The Code Crown!

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.720
Right, right! It's...

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.130
It's all gone...

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.050
I'm only letting you drink

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.320
because you said it 
would jog your memory!

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:38.440
This truly is fine 
tongue-loosening liquor.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.040
I think I'll have some more.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.950
Huh?

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.730
Enough!

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.910
Spit up the location of 
the Code Crown now,

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.190
or you're dead meat!

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.060
No! Not <i>that</i> spit-up!

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:53.950
You...

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.530
It's...

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.290
In here.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.670
Sir Archelomon was captured 
by the Bagramon Army?!

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.170
Don't worry. We'll save him.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.450
Right, Taiki?

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.310
You can bet on it.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.160
Just like ChibiKamemon saved us.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.820
What is that?

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.450
DigiNoir! And it's huge!

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.640
Those guys brought it here?

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.960
But why...

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.680
Master Whamon has awakened!

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:39.670
Whamon?

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.170
This whole island is a 
Digimon called Whamon?!

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.630
Master Whamon awakens once every year,

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.640
at the time of the Summer Festival.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:15.910
That's when we offer 
him lots of DigiNoir,

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:19.760
so he'll protect the 
treasure inside his belly.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.710
Treasure inside his belly?

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.760
It may be the Code Crown.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.040
They plan to use the DigiNoir

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.420
to open Whamon's mouth and get inside?

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.080
That looks so tasty...

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.450
Shoutmon!

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.530
DigiNoir!

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:56.020
We'll paralyze Whamon by 
feeding him explosives,

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.030
then we'll enter his belly 
and find the Code Crown.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.810
Honestly...

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.160
What are they doing?

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.930
Will a plan like this really work?

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.960
Are you okay, Shoutmon?

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.300
Yeah!

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.390
That's awful!

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.140
They were hiding explosives 
among the DigiNoir?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.680
If Whamon eats that, 
there'll be big trouble!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.940
Shakomon! Shoot them down!

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.610
Black Pearl Shot!

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:33.250
Black Pearl Shot!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:37.940
Darn it!

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.320
Shoutmon's giving all he's got so 
Master Whamon won't get hurt...

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.530
Shoutmon...

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.620
That's enough, Shoutmon!

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.020
Taiki!

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.540
Are you okay, Shoutmon?

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:22.930
Taiki...

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.790
Meddling pests!

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.050
We'll have to take care of them first!

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.120
What?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.830
All right! We're going in, too!

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:54.800
It... ate Taiki...

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:06.080
Wow...

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:10.470
So this is what it looks 
like inside Whamon's belly?

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:16.320
Shouldn't we get out 
before he digests us?

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.820
Oh, crap!

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.800
They said the Code Crown is 
in Whamon's belly, right?

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:22.670
Yeah.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.960
Let's look for it, quick!

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:24.920
Got it!

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:31.140
Where are you,

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.160
Code Crown?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.470
Code Crown!

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:40.800
Oh, man!

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.080
Now it'll take forever to find it!

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.790
Oh, yeah!

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.750
Reload, Pickmon!

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.690
Pickmon!

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:55.390
Pickmon, split up and help us find it.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.650
I hope Taiki's okay...

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:55.930
There it is!

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:56.690
So that's it!

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:07.420
You guys...

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:09.230
Return!

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.460
Thanks for saving us the 
effort of searching.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.340
We'll take the Code Crown.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.640
I won't let you!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.130
What is this?

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:25.050
I-I can't move...

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.850
I'll give you my poison 
sting as a little gift.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.900
Once you're stung, you'll be paralyzed,

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.930
your whole body will turn blue, 
and then you'll die.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:47.310
Shoutmon!

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.450
The monsters born in the 
Digital realm: Digimon.

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.670
They may be made up of data,

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:59.000
but they're our precious friends 
who cry, laugh, and fight for us.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:02.060
Join us in our world of adventure

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:05.220
as we gather lots more teammates!

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:06.290
DigiXros!

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:44.760
Shoutmon!

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.910
The Code Crown is ours!

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.490
They're taking too long. 
What's keeping them?

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.910
<i>Master Whamon won't give</i>

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.710
<i>the treasure to outsiders so easily.</i>

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.230
We came all this way,

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.810
and now we can't get the Code Crown?

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.380
Shoutmon, hang in there...

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.990
I hope they're all right...

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:21.330
Shoutmon, Taiki, Sir Archelomon, 
please be okay...

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:24.160
I want everyone to be 
together for the festival.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.770
Please, Master Whamon.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:31.320
Protect them, and protect the island.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.340
Please be safe.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:54.130
I have heard your prayers.

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:56.520
What was that voice?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.930
I am Whamon.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.900
Hold on to me tightly.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:12.980
What?

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.750
You saved us?

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:41.460
Why?

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:44.810
The prayers of those on 
the island reached me.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:46.540
Their prayers?

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.180
That's why you...

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:51.770
Thank you, Whamon.

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:59.040
Whamon, is there any 
way to save Shoutmon?

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.560
He's the kind of Digimon who

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:05.300
would throw his own body at explosives,

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.270
so that you wouldn't eat them by mistake.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:10.430
I know.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:18.510
Rub some of my oil into his wound.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:35.710
Shoutmon!

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.050
Taiki!

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.350
Thank you, Whamon!

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:43.080
You are a human, correct?

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:43.900
Yes.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:48.210
Why do you desire the Code Crown?

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:50.790
If we leave it here, 
the Bagra Army will steal it

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.800
and take control of the island.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:57.370
They tried to take the Code 
Crown even if it meant

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:59.760
killing everyone on the island.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.830
Taiki is our General.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:03.920
He's our savior!

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:06.820
I'm nothing that special...

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:11.110
But all of us in Team Xros 
Heart want to work together

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:14.740
to fight those who do 
bad things to the Digimon.

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:18.140
Work together?

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:22.810
Very well. I will give 
you the Code Crown.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.220
Thank you, Whamon!

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.990
Here, too?

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.300
It appears they got the Code Crown!

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:55.000
Don't fret.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.970
We just have to take back 
what was taken from us.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:13.960
No matter who they may be, 
they can't beat Ebidramon.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.300
Shoutmon!

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.430
Ballistamon!

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.470
DigiXros!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:33.740
Shoutmon!

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.480
Ballistamon!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.090
DigiXros!

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.630
Shoutmon X2!

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:58.660
Starmon!

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:00.440
Pickmons!

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:01.870
DigiXros!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.200
Starmon!

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.630
Pickmons!

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:15.180
Sparkle!

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.960
Star Axe!

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:33.150
Now it's a shrimp?!

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:34.780
Come on, Shoutmon!

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.690
Against Ebidramon,

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:39.990
letting me DigiXros with 
them wouldn't be enough.

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:41.510
What can I do?

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.140
Listen to me.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:50.760
Master Whamon?

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:53.620
Beneath my body is a shrine.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:56.210
There you'll find another treasure.

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.400
Another treasure?

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:00.230
The memories of legendary heroes.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:02.720
They can save you.

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:05.430
The memories of legendary heroes?

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.950
Come on, Shoutmon X2!

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:15.760
If these memories of legendary heroes

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.210
are somewhere under Whamon...

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:23.590
ChibiKamemon went to find 
the other treasure!

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:24.990
ChibiKamemon did?

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:28.430
Try to hang in there until 
ChibiKamemon comes back.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:44.240
<i>There it is!</i>

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:58.860
Water Screw!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.160
Bubbles!

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:05.160
It didn't even leave a mark!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:09.100
Crush him with one blow, Ebidramon!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.380
Use this!

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:24.950
Are these...

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:26.660
They're the memories of the

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:29.240
legendary heroes that Master 
Whamon told us about.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.060
We've got no choice but to try it!

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.700
The one that looks strongest...

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.400
<b>Leviamon</b>

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.400
<b>Attack:</b>

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.400
<b>Rostrum</b>

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.770
...is this one!

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:51.880
Rostrum, activate!

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.720
That's Leviamon!

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:07.000
A Digimon with all the power 
of a Great Demon Lord!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.760
It can't be... 
He should have been destroyed!

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.070
All right!

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:55.240
He did it!

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:56.210
Well done!

00:19:56.210 --> 00:20:00.180
<b>HolyAngemon
Garurumon                    Agumon
MarineAngemon                                                  Leviamon</b>

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:59.120
Awesome! Those are DigiMemories!

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:00.180
DigiMemories?

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.890
Cards that carry the data 
of legendary Digimon!

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:05.620
Wow!

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:09.350
I heard they were hidden somewhere 
in the Digital World.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.420
I guess it really was true!

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:13.660
Legendary Digimon...

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:15.020
That's awesome!

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:18.470
We got not only the Code Crown, 
but the DigiMemories, too!

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:20.230
Talk about luck!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.120
Now I can't let you 
leave the island alive!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:28.370
I won't let a human have the 
Code Crown or the DigiMemories!

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:30.440
Go, Seadramon Army!

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.790
So much for luck...

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:01.910
<b>Monitamon's Lovely♥ Enemy Search</b>

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:01.970
Searching for enemy data.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:02.970
Dondokomon.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.280
Attacks include Dondoko March,

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.960
which raises the spirits 
of friends and foes alike.

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:11.720
<b>[Type]

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:11.720
<b>Musical Instrument</b>

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:11.720
<b>
Dondoko March

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:07.720
Why would you raise the 
enemy's spirits, too?!

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:09.160
Hey, even I'm getting excited!

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.950
Stand up, my friend...

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.070
We are Xros Heart?!

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:18.290
Now it's an army of Seadramon!

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.960
There's no end to them, Taiki!

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.310
We'll get through it with DigiXros!

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:23.940
You've gotta become X3... 
No, X4, Shoutmon!

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:26.060
X4, you say?!

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:27.770
Digimon Xros Wars!

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:29.470
You can't turn your back 
on the next one, either!

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:29.470
<b>X4 Breaks Through the Crisis!</b>
